# Text Size Standards

**WORKSPACE RULE - ALWAYS APPLY**

## Purpose
Ensure consistent, readable text sizing across the application using Tailwind's text utility classes.

## Minimum Text Size Rule

### **Required Standard**
- **All text must be `text-base` (16px) or larger**
- **No `text-xs` (12px) or `text-sm` (14px)** for body content
- **Exception**: Labels, captions, and metadata can use `text-sm` minimum

### **Approved Text Sizes**

#### **Primary Content**
```tsx
// ✅ REQUIRED - Use these for main content
text-base    // 16px - Minimum for body text
text-lg      // 18px - Emphasized content
text-xl      // 20px - Section headers
text-2xl     // 24px - Page titles
text-3xl     // 30px - Main headings
```

#### **Secondary Content** 
```tsx
// ✅ ALLOWED - Use sparingly for metadata only
text-sm      // 14px - Labels, captions, helper text
```

#### **Forbidden Sizes**
```tsx
// ❌ NEVER USE - Too small for accessibility
text-xs      // 12px - Prohibited
text-[11px]  // Custom small sizes - Prohibited
```

## Implementation Guidelines

### **Component Text Sizing**

#### **Form Elements**
```tsx
// ✅ Input labels
<label className="text-base font-medium text-gray-700">
  Email Address
</label>

// ✅ Input fields
<input className="text-base px-3 py-2 border rounded-md" />

// ✅ Helper text (exception - can use text-sm)
<p className="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">
  We'll never share your email
</p>
```

#### **Navigation & Buttons**
```tsx
// ✅ Navigation links
<a className="text-base font-medium text-gray-900">
  Manuscripts
</a>

// ✅ Button text
<button className="text-base font-medium px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white">
  Save Changes
</button>
```

#### **Content Areas**
```tsx
// ✅ Body paragraphs
<p className="text-base text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
  Main content text goes here...
</p>

// ✅ List items
<li className="text-base text-gray-700">
  List item content
</li>
```

#### **Headers & Titles**
```tsx
// ✅ Page titles
<h1 className="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">
  Page Title
</h1>

// ✅ Section headers
<h2 className="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">
  Section Title
</h2>

// ✅ Card titles
<h3 className="text-lg font-medium text-gray-900">
  Card Title
</h3>
```

### **Acceptable Exceptions**

#### **Metadata & Labels**
```tsx
// ✅ Status badges (can use text-sm)
<span className="text-sm px-2 py-1 bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 rounded-full">
  Published
</span>

// ✅ Timestamps (can use text-sm)
<span className="text-sm text-gray-500">
  Created 2 hours ago
</span>

// ✅ Field labels (can use text-sm)
<label className="text-sm font-medium text-gray-600">
  Optional Field
</label>
```

#### **Dense Data Tables**
```tsx
// ✅ Table headers (minimum text-sm)
<th className="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wide">
  Column Header
</th>

// ✅ Table cells (prefer text-base, text-sm acceptable)
<td className="text-base text-gray-900">
  Cell Content
</td>
```

## Accessibility Considerations

### **WCAG Compliance**
- **16px minimum** meets WCAG AA standards
- **Larger text** improves readability for all users
- **Consistent sizing** reduces cognitive load

### **Responsive Scaling**
```tsx
// ✅ Scale text appropriately on mobile
<h1 className="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold">
  Responsive Title
</h1>

<p className="text-base md:text-lg">
  Responsive body text
</p>
```

## Code Review Checklist

### **Before Committing**
- [ ] All body text uses `text-base` or larger
- [ ] No `text-xs` classes in the codebase
- [ ] `text-sm` only used for metadata/labels
- [ ] Headings use appropriate hierarchy (`text-xl`, `text-2xl`, `text-3xl`)
- [ ] Form elements have readable text sizes

### **Common Violations to Fix**
```tsx
// ❌ Fix these patterns
<p className="text-sm">Main content</p>          // Use text-base
<button className="text-xs">Click me</button>    // Use text-base
<div className="text-[12px]">Content</div>       // Use text-base
<span className="text-sm">Important info</span>  // Use text-base (unless metadata)
```

## Migration Strategy

### **Existing Code Cleanup**
1. **Search for violations**: `grep -r "text-xs\|text-sm" src/`
2. **Evaluate each usage**: Is this metadata or main content?
3. **Upgrade to text-base**: For all main content
4. **Keep text-sm**: Only for true metadata/labels

### **Component Updates**
```tsx
// Before (❌)
<div className="text-sm text-gray-600">
  This is important user content that should be readable
</div>

// After (✅)
<div className="text-base text-gray-600">
  This is important user content that should be readable
</div>
```

## Enforcement

### **ESLint Rule** (if available)
```json
{
  "rules": {
    "tailwind/no-small-text": "error"
  }
}
```

### **Manual Review Process**
- **Every PR** must verify text sizing
- **Search for** `text-xs` and flag for removal
- **Justify** any `text-sm` usage in PR description

